['Here's an example of how you might implement this in Java:

```java
import android.content.Context;
import android.graphics.Bitmap;
import android.os.Environment;
import android.util.Log;

import java.io.*;

public class ThemeManager {
    private static final String TAG = "ThemeManager";

    // Singleton instance
    private static volatile ThemeManager instance;

    // Default theme directory and caching root
    private File defaultThemeDirectory, cacheRoot;

    // Synchronization lock
    private final Object lock = new Object();

    public static ThemeManager getInstance(Context context) {
        if (instance == null) {
            synchronized (ThemeManager.class) {
                if (instance == null) {
                    instance = new ThemeManager(context);
                }
            }
        }
        return instance;
    }

    private ThemeManager(Context context) {
        // Initialize default theme directory and caching root
        this.defaultThemeDirectory = getDefaultThemeDir();
        this.cacheRoot = context.getCacheDir();

        if (!this.defaultThemeDirectory.exists()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Default theme directory does not exist");
        }
    }

    public MoSTState loadState(String filePath, Bitmap themeBitmap) {
        synchronized (lock) {
            // Recycle the bitmap before loading a new state
            if (themeBitmap != null && !themeBitmap.isRecycled()) {
                themeBitmap.recycle();
                themeBitmap = null;
            }

            File fileToRead = new File(filePath);

            // Check if the file exists and is not a directory
            if (fileToRead.exists() && !fileToRead.isDirectory()) {
                try (FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream(fileToRead);
                     ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(fis)) {
                    return (MoSTState) ois.readObject();
                } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
                    Log.e(TAG, "Error loading state", e);
                }
            } else {
                Log.w(TAG, "File not found: " + filePath);
            }
        }

        return null; // Return null if the object is not a MoSTState or an error occurred
    }

    public Bitmap loadBitmapFromCache() {
        File[] files = cacheRoot.listFiles();

        if (files != null) {
            for (File file : files) {
                // Check if the file is a PNG image
                if (file.getName().endsWith(".png")) {
                    return BitmapFactory.decodeFile(file.getAbsolutePath());
                }
            }
        }

        return null; // Return null if no PNG file was found in the cache
    }

    private File getDefaultThemeDir() {
        String externalStorageState = Environment.getExternalStorageState();

        // Check if external storage is available and writable
        if (Environment.MEDIA_MOUNTED.equals(externalStorageState)) {
            return new File(Environment.getExternalStorageDirectory(), "defaultThemeDir");
        } else {
            return context.getFilesDir();
        }
    }
}
```

The `loadBitmapFromCache()` method demonstrates a strategy for parsing files from the cache and caching them to optimize performance in subsequent accesses. 

Remember to replace `"defaultThemeDir"` with your desired default theme directory name. This code also assumes that the serialized file is stored on external storage or within the application's private data directory, depending on external storage availability.

For better performance and error recovery, consider using a more sophisticated method for parsing and caching files, possibly utilizing libraries like Picasso or Glide. For error handling, you might want to provide more detailed information about errors to help debugging in production environments. Additionally, ensure that your `ThemeManager` class is appropriately synchronized when used across multiple threads or from different methods to prevent race conditions.
']

