This function is designed to easily support other data formats as long as they can fit into a stream - if you have to work with different types of data, the function could be split up into several smaller ones each responsible for their own type of data. This approach would make it easier to add additional integrations or change behavior later on.

This solution is also designed around a "pull" model where the consumer decides when and how much data they want - this is in contrast to a traditional "push" model where data is sent over time. However, if you need a push-based system, you might look into libraries like `highland` that provide this kind of functionality.
