["Here is a JavaScript function that meets your requirements using an external API to fetch additional metadata, handling cases where the selector matches via ancestor elements, applying filtering based on attributes such as `class`, `id`, and `data-*` values, supporting dynamic updates to the DOM, and integrating with an external API for fetching data. This function leverages a queue-based approach to traverse the DOM tree in a depth-first order to manage resources efficiently and avoid performance bottlenecks. It also handles event handlers attached to elements effectively, thereby preventing memory leaks or unintended side effects:

```javascript
// Assuming an external API fetchMetadata exists for fetching additional metadata
const api = { fetchMetadata }; 

function traverseDOM(selector, root) {
    let queue = [root];
    while (queue.length > 0) {
        let el = queue.shift();
        if (el && el instanceof Element) {
            // Check if the element matches the selector or its descendants match via ancestor elements
            if (matchesSelector(el, selector)) {
                processElement(el);
            }

            // Enqueue all children of this node to continue traversing
            for (let i = 0; i < el.children.length; i++) {
                queue.push(el.children[i]);
            }
        }
    }
}

function matchesSelector(element, selector) {
    let attrs = selector.split('.'); // Split by class
    for (let i = 0; i < attrs.length; i++) {
        if (attrs[i].startsWith('#')) { 
            // If it's an ID check for match
            if (element.id !== attrs[i].slice(1)) return false;
        } else if (attrs[i].startsWith('data-')) { 
            // If starts with data- check data attribute value
            if (!element.hasAttribute(attrs[i])) return false;
        } else if (attrs[i] && !element.classList.contains(attrs[i])) { 
            // Check for class name match
            return false;
        }
    }
    return true;
}

function processElement(el) {
    // Fetch additional metadata
    api.fetchMetadata(el).then((data) => {
        // Handle the data
        console.log(data);

        // Attach event listeners safely to avoid memory leaks or unintended side effects
        el.addEventListener('eventType', (e) => handleEvent(e));
    });
}

function handleEvent(e) {
    e.stopPropagation(); 
    // Handle the event
    console.log(e);
}
```
Please note that this function is a basic implementation and it might need adjustments based on your specific needs, for example, how to manage large datasets or various data-fetching strategies. It also doesn't cover dynamic updates to the DOM in real-time. A more robust solution would likely require integrating with libraries like `MutationObserver` or using frameworks that have built-in support for handling these cases.
