    record->message = malloc(sizeof(char) * messageLength);
    if (record->message == NULL) {
        free(record); // Failed to allocate memory, clean up
        return NULL;
    }

    strncpy(record->message, template[index], messageLength);

    record->config_param = rand() % (max - min + 1) + min;
    return record;
}

void free_log_record(LogRecord *record) {
    if (record != NULL) {
        free(record->message);
        free(record);
    }
}
``` 

This code provides a basic structure for log records. It uses dynamic memory allocation to create a new record with a given offset and a randomly chosen message from an array of templates. The configuration parameter is also initialized to a random value within the specified range.

