It uses locks for mutual exclusion when accessing the cache. The `atomic_fetch_add` function is used to safely increment the hit count without causing any data races or race conditions. 
The code doesn't include a method to fetch events from a database, as this will depend on the specifics of the system and would likely involve network calls or other I/O operations. It also assumes that `TrafficEvent` is already defined elsewhere in your program, and it frees the memory for each location field before assigning new data to it to avoid memory leaks.
